---
layout: base.njk
title: "Motorcycle Fuel Range Calculator"
description: "Calculate exactly how far you can ride on a full tank. Enter your bike's tank size and fuel consumption to plan your ride."
permalink: /tools/fuel-range-calculator/
---
<script src="{{ '/js/bike-lookup.js' | url }}"></script>

<div class="tool-page">
  <div>
    <h1>Motorcycle Fuel Range Calculator</h1>
    <p class="tool-intro">Find out exactly how far you can ride before hitting reserve. Look up your bike to auto-fill the tank size, then enter your consumption to get your range.</p>

    <div class="tool-layout">
      <aside class="tool-sidebar"><div class="ad-slot"><!-- AdSense 160×600 --></div></aside>
      <div class="tool-main">
        <div class="tool-card">
          <!-- LIVE API LOOKUP -->
          <h2>Find Your Bike</h2>
          <div id="bike-finder-fuel" class="api-lookup-block"></div>
          <div class="selector-row" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
            <div class="form-group">
              <label>Unit</label>
              <select id="api-fuel-unit">
                <option value="litres" selected>Litres</option>
                <option value="gallons">US Gallons</option>
              </select>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2>Tank &amp; Consumption</h2>
          <div class="selector-row">
            <div class="form-group"><label>Tank Size (litres)</label><input type="number" id="tank" value="15" min="3" max="50" step="0.1"></div>
            <div class="form-group"><label>Reserve (litres)</label><input type="number" id="reserve" value="2.5" min="0.5" max="10" step="0.1"></div>
            <div class="form-group"><label>Consumption (L/100km)</label><input type="number" id="cons" value="5.5" min="2" max="20" step="0.1"></div>
          </div>

          <button class="btn-calculate" onclick="calcFuel()">Calculate Range</button>

          <div id="results" class="results" style="display:none">
            <h2>Range Results</h2>
            <div class="range-cards">
              <div class="range-card green"><div class="range-label">Full Tank</div><div class="range-value" id="r-full-km">—</div><div class="range-sub" id="r-full-mi">—</div></div>
              <div class="range-card orange"><div class="range-label">To Reserve</div><div class="range-value" id="r-res-km">—</div><div class="range-sub" id="r-res-mi">—</div></div>
              <div class="range-card red"><div class="range-label">Reserve Only</div><div class="range-value" id="r-only-km">—</div><div class="range-sub" id="r-only-mi">—</div></div>
            </div>
            <p class="results-note">Manufacturer figures measured under ideal conditions. Real-world range varies with speed, load and riding style.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tool-seo">
          <h2>How to Use the Motorcycle Fuel Range Calculator</h2>
          <p>Look up your bike to auto-fill tank size, or enter your own values. The calculator shows your total range on a full tank, how far you can ride before hitting reserve, and how far the reserve fuel will carry you. Always plan fuel stops at 80% of the calculated range.</p>
          <h2>Tips for Maximising Range</h2>
          <p>Steady speeds between 80–100 km/h give the best fuel economy. High speeds, hard acceleration, cold weather and heavy luggage all increase consumption significantly. For long-distance touring, use your actual consumption from past rides rather than the manufacturer figure.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="tool-sidebar"><div class="ad-slot"><!-- AdSense 160×600 --></div></aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
